+### Review protocol: `compact` (default) vs `strict` (opt-in)
+
+| | compact | strict |
+|---|---|---|
+| Labels | fixed seat order → Response A, B, C… | shuffled per deliberation |
+| Who reviews | every member reviews ALL answers, its own included | no member ever reviews its own answer (or the judge reviews all) |
+| Ranking parse | lenient (numbered lines, else bare `Response X` mentions) | complete permutation of the labels shown, or **one** corrective retry, then the review is **discarded** and counted as a failure |
+| Stakes | `MATERIAL FLAW:` lines requested | a `MATERIAL FLAW:` line or `No material flaws found.` is **required** |
+| Aggregation | average rank (omitted label = worst+1) | first-place votes first, average rank as tie-break, averaged only over reviewers shown the label |
+| Calls | `2N+1` with peer review | up to `N + 2N + 1` (each review may retry once); with `max_calls` set and too small, strict **downgrades visibly** to compact |
+
+Strict is not "fresh reviewers": Stage-2 reviewers are still the Stage-1 seats,
+just never on their own answer. Both protocols, at no extra calls: members check
+the premise and end with `Confidence:` + `Flip condition:`; reviewers write
+stake-weighted `MATERIAL FLAW:` lines, which the chairman's guidance keeps
+**regardless of ranking**; the chairman is asked to reconcile consensus, dissent,
+failures, confidence, the strongest flip condition and one falsifier; and the
+guidance carries a call summary (calls made, valid rankings, failures).
+
+**Privacy:** every member, reviewer and judge message, and the chairman guidance,
+pass through Hermes' fail-closed egress scrub (`agent.redact.redact_for_egress`)
+before leaving the process. The chairman's own conversation is sent like any
+normal model turn. Members and reviewers never receive tools; only the chairman
+can act — unlike dev-pair, whose single reviewer is permanently tool-less.
+
